Which is 28 bytes. The WGSL spec says that the size of a struct is rounded up to the next multiple of 16. So 28 rounds up to 32. So the Rust struct should also be 32 bytes. So adding a 4-byte padding at the end.

Alternatively, we can use `#[repr(align(16))]` but it's simpler to add padding.

